  "id": "COMPOUND:24149 - PROTEIN:5856",
  "verbalization": "Mexogenin appears to interact with SNU-387 through a series of molecular targets that are all involved in the regulation of microtubules. The evidence suggests that Mexogenin acts as a target for multiple compounds, including Microtubule-associated protein 1B, which in turn is a target of several other molecules such as Sasanquasaponin I, 4-Fluorobenzoic acid, tridec-2-ynyl ester, and 3-O-Methyl Droserone. These compounds are all known to influence microtubule dynamics, which implies a potential role in the cellular processes that SNU-387 may target. The integration of these pathways highlights a possible mechanism by which Mexogenin could modulate SNU-387's activity, likely through the modulation of microtubule-associated proteins. The shared involvement of microtubule-related targets across different compounds suggests a broader functional relationship, though the exact nature of the interaction remains to be fully elucidated.",
